# Git workflow

## Branches

- Primary: `main`
- Feature / fix branches: short prefix + topic (`feat/…`, `fix/…`, `cursor/…`, `docs/…`)
- Prefer atomic commits; open PRs against `main`

## Commits (hybrid recommendation)

Prefer Conventional Commits (already common in recent history):

```
feat(scope): …
fix(scope): …
docs(scope): …
chore(scope): …
```

Scopes often match packages/apps: `desktop`, `mobile`, `cli`, `knowledge`, `gateway`, etc.

## Versioning

- Semantic versioning via tags (`v0.x.y`); Release workflow syncs from the tag
- Do not bump packaging versions casually — follow `docs/ci-and-releases.md`

## Agent constraints

- Commit only when the user asks (unless `/ship` / roadmap ship rules apply)
- No force-push to `main`; no `--no-verify` unless explicitly requested
- Validate with `bun run validate` before pushing when feasible
